Smart City Infrastructure Optimization using AI, IoT, and Blockchain
Overview
This project demonstrates a scalable Smart City platform designed to optimize urban infrastructure using AI, IoT, and Blockchain technologies. It enables real-time monitoring, predictive maintenance, and citizen engagement, empowering city administrators to make data-driven decisions for sustainable urban development.
Key Features
•	Real-Time Traffic Monitoring — Uses IoT sensors and AI models to detect congestion and optimize traffic flow.
•	Smart Waste Management — Predicts waste collection needs and routes for maximum efficiency.
•	Predictive Maintenance — Forecasts potential utility failures using machine learning models.
•	Citizen Portal — Web interface for citizens to report issues and track resolution progress.
•	Data Dashboards — Visual analytics for administrators built with Power BI and Node-RED.
•	Blockchain Security Layer — Ensures transparent, tamper-proof transaction logs and audit trails.
System Architecture
[ IoT Devices ] → [ MQTT Broker / Node-RED ] → [ Backend (Node.js/Flask) ] → [ Database (MongoDB/PostgreSQL) ] → [ Power BI Dashboards ] → [ Blockchain (Ethereum)]
Technology Stack
IoT & Edge: Raspberry Pi, Arduino, Node-RED, MQTT
AI & ML: Python, Scikit-learn, TensorFlow, Pandas
Backend: Node.js, Express, Flask
Blockchain: Ethereum, Solidity
Database: MongoDB, PostgreSQL
Visualization: Power BI
Cloud/Deployment: AWS IoT Core, EC2, Docker
Dashboards & Analytics
Built interactive Power BI dashboards for visualizing live data streams and integrated Node-RED alert systems for real-time notifications to city officials.
Blockchain Integration
Implemented Ethereum-based smart contracts to securely store service requests and transaction records, ensuring data immutability, traceability, and public accountability.
Impact
•	Improved city service efficiency by 35% through automation and predictive analytics.
•	Enhanced transparency and citizen satisfaction via blockchain-based feedback tracking.
•	Reduced maintenance costs and downtime for public utilities.
